  "worked_solution": "Notice that our sentence can be re-phrased as \n\nFor any real number $x,$ we have that ${x}^{2}$ is a non-negative number.\n\nNow, \"${x}^{2}$ is a non-negative number\" means that\n\nThere exists a non-negative number $y$ such that ${x}^{2}=y.$\n\nTherefore, we get the following statement:\n\nFor any real number $x,$ there exists a non-negative number $y$ such that ${x}^{2}=y.$\n\nMore formally, this reads as\n\n$\u2200\\,x\\in R,\\,\u2203\\,y\\in {R}_{0}^{+},\\,{x}^{2}=y.$",
